{number: 64}
{title: Only Trust Him}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Come, every soul by sin oppressed,
There's mercy with the [D7] Lord,
And [G] He will surely give you rest
By [D7] trusting in His [G] Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G] Only trust Him, only trust Him,
Only trust Him [D7] now;
He [G] will save you, He will save you,
He will [D7] save you [G] now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
For [G] Jesus shed His precious blood
Rich blessings to be-[D7] stow;
Plunge [G] now into the crimson flood
That [D7] washes white as [G] snow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Yes, [G] Jesus is the Truth, the Way,
That leads you into [D7] rest;
Be-[G] lieve in Him without delay,
And [D7] you are fully [G] blest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Come [G] then, and join this holy band,
And on to glory [D7] go,
To [G] dwell in that celestial land,
Where [D7] joys immortal [G] flow.
{end_of_verse}
